{{Quote|I do love the capital. It's a masterful expression of our architecture.|[[Alrich Wren]]|<ref name="Heroes of Mandalore">{{Rebels|Heroes of Mandalore}}</ref>}}
'''Sundari''' was the [[Domed city|domed]] [[capital]] [[city]] of the [[planet]] [[Mandalore]].<ref name="TMP Episode Gallery">{{SW|url=series/clone-wars/the-mandalore-plot-episode-gallery|text="The Mandalore Plot" Episode Gallery}}</ref> The city was situated in the [[desert]]s of Mandalore and was enclosed by a [[Bio-cube|bio-dome]] that allowed the city to exist on the harsh planet, which had been [[Annihilation|rendered]] a desert after [[Standard year|years]] of [[Mandalorian]] wars. During the reign of the pacifist [[New Mandalorians|New Mandalorian]] government, led by [[Duchess]] [[Satine Kryze]], the city was the site of multiple attacks by the splinter faction known as [[Death Watch]].<ref name="The Mandalore Plot" /> They eventually took over the city during the [[Clone Wars]] in an effort to restore Mandalore to its warrior past.<ref name="Shades of Reason" /> Shortly thereafter, it was the site of a [[Mandalorian Civil War (19 BBY)|civil war]] between different Death Watch factions, who were fighting as a result of the rogue [[Sith]] [[Sith Lord|Lord]] [[Maul]]'s [[Takeover of Mandalore|takeover]] of Death Watch.<ref name="The Lawless" />

After being the center of the [[Galactic Empire]]'s [[occupation of Mandalore]],<ref name="Heroes of Mandalore" /> Sundari was destroyed in the [[Night of a Thousand Tears]].<ref name="BOBF" />

==Description==
[[File:Peace_Park.png|thumb|left|250px|The interior of the domed city of Sundari was full of beautiful architecture.]]
Situated in a desert,<ref name="Ultimate Star Wars, New Edition" /> Sundari was a massive<ref name="Collapse of the Republic">''[[Collapse of the Republic]]''</ref> [[bio-cube]] [[city]], and the [[capital]] city of the [[New Mandalorians]].<ref name="Ultimate Star Wars, New Edition">''[[Ultimate Star Wars, New Edition]]''</ref> Sundari enclosed one of Mandalore's largest active [[Mining|mines]] of [[beskar]] within its outer walls, providing the city with valuable resources and a major strategic asset.<ref name="FLT">''[[Friends Like These]]''</ref> The entrance to these mines were located below the [[Civic Center]] in the [[capital]] [[city]], Sundari.<ref name="Chapter 17">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 17: The Apostate}}</ref> Below the [[Mines of Mandalore]] were the [[Living Waters]]. According to the [[Mandalorian Creed]], a Mandalorian who took off their helmet could seek atonement by bathing in the Living Waters.<ref name="BOBF" />

Within the dome, Sundari was a multilevel city with individual towering structures<ref name="Collapse of the Republic" /> made of [[permacrete]] and [[transparisteel]].<ref name="BMF 32">{{BuildFalconCite|32|Guide to the Galaxy}}</ref> It was a shimmering example of the unique translucent architectural style prevalent on Mandalore. Transparent and translucent panels and windows were extremely common features, often arranged in geometric patterns. Many bridges and floors were also transparent, making it possible to see up and down through the buildings and other structures as much as through any window.<ref name="Collapse of the Republic" />

==History==
===Clone Wars===
====Pillar of neutrality====
[[File:New_Mandalorians.png|thumb|right|250px|Duchess Satine Kryze ruled Mandalore from Sundari during the beginning of the war]]
In [[21 BBY]],<ref name="Atlas">''[[Star Wars: Galactic Atlas]]''</ref> during the [[Clone Wars]], [[Jedi Master]] [[Obi-Wan Kenobi]] was sent to Sundari. He investigated rumors about the [[New Mandalorians]]' leader, [[Duchess]] [[Satine Kryze]], leading [[Mandalore]] in joining the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems]] following an [[Attack on a Republic cruiser|attack]] on a [[Galactic Republic|Republic]] [[cruiser]]. The Duchess informed Kenobi that a movement called the [[Death Watch]] was behind the attack and in collaboration with the Separatists. [[Death]] Watch then staged a [[Attack on the Memorial Shrine|bombing]] on the [[Peace Park]]'s [[Memorial Shrine]]. Kenobi found the [[Death Watch bomber|bomber]], but the bomber chose to jump to [[Death|his death]].<ref name="The Mandalore Plot" />

A [[parade]] was held to honor the arrival of [[Naboo]]'s [[Senator]], [[Padmé Amidala Naberrie|Padmé Amidala]]. During this [[time]], several [[Moogan]] [[smuggler]]s [[Mandalorian black market conspiracy|brought]] in [[Ardees Beverage]] [[tea]]. The smugglers inadvertently diluted and [[poison]]ed the tea with [[slabin]] resulting in an outbreak of illness among schoolchildren across the [[planet]]. Fortunately, Amidala, Kryze and [[Journeyman Protector|her bodyguards]] put an [[Skirmish at the Sundari docks|end]] to this [[Mooga smuggling ring|smuggling ring]].<ref name="Corruption" /> After it was discovered that Mandalore's [[Prime Minister|prime minister]], [[Almec]] and the [[Mandalorian secret service|secret service]] were behind the smuggling, he was arrested by Kryze, [[Jedi]] [[Padawan]] [[Ahsoka Tano]], and [[Korkie Kryze]]'s fellow [[cadet]]s.<ref name="The Academy" />

Sundari was later chosen as a neutral location for [[Confederate–Republic peace conference|negotiations]] between the Republic and the Confederacy. However, it came to an end when Tano rescued former [[Onderon]] Senator [[Lux Bonteri]] from [[Dooku]]'s executioners. A firefight broke between the [[Commando Droid Diplomat|commando droids]] and [[Captain]] [[Taggart (Senate Guard)|Taggart's]] [[Senate Guard]]s.<ref name="AFiN">{{TCW|A Friend in Need}}</ref>

====Maul's vision====
[[File:Epguide515.png|thumb|left|275px|Death Watch successfully overthrew the pacifist regime]]
After the former [[Sith apprentice]] [[Maul]] was [[Mission to Lotho Minor|rescued]] by his brother [[Savage Opress]]<ref name="Brothers">{{TCW|Brothers (episode)}}</ref> and [[Magick|healed]] by [[Mother (title)|Mother]] [[Talzin]],<ref name="Revenge">{{TCW|Revenge (episode)}}</ref> the two renegade Sith brothers eventually set their eyes on Mandalore, assembling the [[Shadow Collective]], which included allies such as [[Black Sun]], the [[Pyke Syndicate]], and most importantly, [[Pre Vizsla]] and [[Death Watch]]. Maul devised a plan to conquer Mandalore,<ref name="Eminence">{{TCW|Eminence (episode)}}</ref> invading Sundari with their criminal forces and staging Death Watch soldiers to liberate them, turning what was once a terrorist group in the eyes of the public into their liberators. Vizsla would ascend to Mandalore's ruler before he was slain by Maul in single combat, who claimed the [[Darksaber]] and installed the formerly disgraced prime minister Almec as the public figurehead of his reign.<ref name="Shades">{{TCW|Shades of Reason}}</ref>

Maul also executed Duchess Satine. However, when he was defeated by [[Darth Sidious]], who viewed Maul as a significant threat,<ref name="Lawless">{{TCW|The Lawless}}</ref> Almec retained his power over Sundari and Mandalore.<ref name="Old Friends">{{TCW|Old Friends Not Forgotten}}</ref> Maul would later be rescued by [[Gar Saxon]] and [[Rook Kast]] from prison on [[Stygeon Prime]],<ref name="SonOfDathomir1">[[Darth Maul — Son of Dathomir 1|''Darth Maul — Son of Dathomir'' 1]]</ref> and, after re-gathering his allies, returned to Sundari, which he used as his base of operations to execute his machinations across the galaxy.<ref name="Old Friends" />

====The war arrives====
[[File:RookKastLeadsTheCharge.png|thumb|right|250px|Maul's forces fighting the 332nd in the center of the city]]
Eventually, [[Bo-Katan Kryze]], a former Death Watch [[lieutenant]] who left the group after Maul's takeover, recruited [[Galactic Republic]] forces to assist her in ousting Maul. Joined by former Jedi Padawan Ahsoka Tano, recently promoted [[Clone Commander]] [[Rex]], and the [[332nd Division]], their forces landed at Sundari and engaged in a bloody [[Siege of Mandalore|battle]] against Maul and his [[Mandalorian super commando]]s.<ref name="Old Friends" /> Maul's forces would be beaten back, but Maul, sensing the impending [[Great Jedi Purge|chaos]] that would be set upon the galaxy, attempted one last act, luring Tano to the Sundari palace in an attempt to recruit her to his side and stop the violence he foresaw. However, Tano refused to join him, and she defeated him in a duel and captured him as Maul's remaining forces were defeated in the city.<ref name="Phantom" />

Republic forces remained in Sundari after the battle was over,<ref name="Shattered">{{TCW|Shattered}}</ref> and after [[Order 66]] and the [[Proclamation of the New Order|proclamation]] of the new [[Galactic Empire]], Sundari was occupied by the new regime.<ref name="Protector Recon">{{RebelsRecon|Ob90p0SoMpY|#2.19: Inside "The Mystery of Chopper Base" &#124; Star Wars Rebels|sw_url=video/rebels-recon-inside-the-mystery-of-chopper-base}}</ref>

===Imperial Era===
[[File:Sundari_HoM1.png|thumb|left|250px|Sundari during the Imperial Era]]
During the [[early rebellion against the Galactic Empire]], [[Galactic Empire|Imperial]] [[Governor]] [[Tiber Saxon]] had his [[Tiber Saxon's Star Destroyer|command ship]] above Sundari during a [[Mandalorian Civil War (Imperial Era)|civil war]]. The ship was [[Mission to Mandalore|destroyed]] by [[Alliance to Restore the Republic|Rebel]] [[Spectres|forces]] that were allied with [[Clan Kryze]] and [[Clan Wren]].<ref name="Heroes of Mandalore" />

Various [[Mandalorian clan]]s banded together to fight the Empire as the [[Mandalorian resistance]].<ref name="Heroes of Mandalore" /> Understanding that they would be unable to control Mandalore, the Empire launched the [[Great Purge of Mandalore]] against the Mandalorians.<ref name="Chapter 11">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 11: The Heiress}}</ref> During the [[Night of a Thousand Tears]], flights of [[TIE/sa tactical bomber|TIE/sa bombers]] bombed the domed cities on Mandalore, including Sundari, while [[KX-series security droid]]s and [[Viper probe droid|probe droids]] scoured the urban wrecks to kill any survivors.<ref name="BOBF" />

===New Republic Era===
[[File:Massacre-on-Mandalore.png|thumb|right|290px|Sundari was laid waste by the Empire.]]
In [[9 ABY]]<ref name="Date">{{MandoDate|18}}</ref>, the Mandalorian bounty hunter, [[Din Djarin]] and [[Din Grogu|Grogu]] landed outside of Sundari's ruins. Djarin and [[R5-D4]] were attacked by [[Alamite]]s who had moved into the ruins.<ref name="Mines of Mandalore">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 18: The Mines of Mandalore}}</ref>

A picture of Sundari from when Maul planned his takeover of Mandalore was in "[[Index of Organizations]]," a survival compendium sent out by [[Carson Teva]] during the [[New Republic Era]].<ref name="Organizations">{{GermanFanCite|116|Database}}</ref> Sundari was also mentioned in "[[Mandalorians Through the Ages]]," a publication by the [[historian]] [[Eloc Throno]], which described Sundari's history and events during the Clone Wars.<ref name="Not a Mandalorian Like Any Other">{{GermanFanCite|106|Database}}</ref>

